      "label": "Local Government Boundaries Commission for Northern Ireland: Provisional Recommendations (1971)",
      "note": "Provisional stage of the review under the Local Government (Boundaries) Act (Northern Ireland) 1971, with proposed district and ward names and electors; final recommendations followed in 1972. Printed report (HMSO); no online copy found."
    },
    {
      "label": "Local Government (Boundaries) Order (Northern Ireland) 1972 (S.R. & O. 1972 No. 131)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/nisro/1972/131/contents/made",
      "note": "Made 20 Jun 1972, in force 17 Jul 1972; gives effect without modification to the recommendations the Local Government Boundaries Commissioner submitted on 25 Apr 1972 under section 4 of the Local Government (Boundaries) Act (Northern Ireland) 1971. Schedule 2 lists each district's wards by townland. The districts took up their functions after the 1973 local elections."
    },
    {
      "label": "Local Government (Boundaries) Act (Northern Ireland) 1971 (1971 c. 9)",
      "url": "https://www.legislation.gov.uk/apni/1971/9",
      "note": "Royal Assent 23 Mar 1971. Provided for the new local government districts, each to include the whole or major part of one of the places listed in Schedule 1, and for their division into wards, on the recommendations of a Local Government Boundaries Commissioner; section 4 provided for giving effect to them by order, which the Local Government (Boundaries) Order (Northern Ireland) 1972 did. Repealed from 1 Apr 2015 by the Local Government (Boundaries) Act (Northern Ireland) 2008."
    }
